WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
Pilton, Somerset.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.710
In 1970, Glastonbury Festival began
here as a small event on a dairy farm.

3
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:14.330
Today, its licence allows up to 210,000
people aged 13 or over at each event.

4
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:19.250
The festival tells traders to expect
over 200,000 people at the busiest time,

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.790
on about 900 acres.

6
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.830
Then everyone leaves,
and it's a farm again.

7
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.010
Do the organisers take all the gains?

8
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.450
Does nobody pay, as it's temporary?

9
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.770
Who gains, and who pays?

10
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.930
In this mission, you'll map
Glastonbury's site and situation,

11
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.830
from roads to water and power.

12
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:41.210
Then you'll test a claim
of 168 million pounds,

13
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.010
and ask who paid for the study.

14
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.650
Your mission: weigh up who
gains from the festival,

15
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.200
and who pays.
